\ Strict-mode rejection of `pragma-get?`: a row-variable word whose body
\ underflows the abstract stack in a way the row-underflow fallback deliberately
\ does not model (the row does not sit at the bottom slot it can settle). It must
\ stay uncompilable, so calling it from compiled code surfaces as a build error
\ in --interpreter-fallback=false mode, naming `pragma-get?` as the compound
\ callee. This guards the fallback against future over-broadening.
some-pragma: pragma-get? drop
